// F47, the subtle one: Result's constructors are the lowercase functions ok()/err(), while Ok/Err
// are its variant names in a switch arm. A model that found `Ok(v)` in a switch and reached for
// `Ok(1)` to build one gets told the difference, rather than being pointed at `Result<...> { }`,
// which does not parse.
fn main() {
    val r = result(1)
    print(1)
}
